On X, Seattle also shared a photo of Eras Tour-style friendship bracelets reading, &#8220;Seahawks win,&#8221; captioned with &#8220;End Game,&#8221; the title of one of Swift&#8217;s Reputation singles.

Though the 14-time Grammy winner wasn&#8217;t in attendance at the Chiefs vs. Seahawks matchup, she has been at every Kansas City home game so far this season. On Oct. 18, famous friends Este Haim and Caitlin Clark joined Swift in her usual suite with Donna and Ed Kelce as they cheered the Chiefs on against the Los Angeles Chargers.

The singer has been staying busy as usual lately, releasing The Life of a Showgirl: The Encore in September and logging a 16th Billboard Hot 100 No. 1 with one of the deluxe songs, &#8220;Patient Zero.&#8221; About a week ago, she attended the Academy Museum Gala and performed a handful of songs including her Toy Story 5 soundtrack hit &#8220;I Knew It, I Knew You.&#8221;

